{title: 138 - Rise Up, Shepherd, and Follow}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #138 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 138}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]There’s a star in the [G]east on [A]Christmas [D]morn.
Rise up, [C]shepherd, [G]and [A7]follow.
[D]It will lead to the [G]place and where the [D]Sav[G]iour’s [Bm]born,
[D7]Rise up, [Em]shepherd, and [A7]fol[D]low.
[D]Leave your sheep and [G]leave your [D]lambs,
[D]Rise up, [C]shepherd, [G]and [A7]follow.
[D]Leave your ewes and [G]leave your [D]rams,
[D7]Rise up, [Em]shepherd, [G]and [A7]fol[D]low.
[D]Follow, follow,
Rise up [C]shepherd, [G]and [A7]follow.
[D]Follow the star of [G]Beth[A]le[Bm]hem,
[D7]Rise up, [Em]shepherd, [G]and [A7]fol[D]low.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Leave [G]your sheep [A]and leave [D]your lamb,
[C]Rise [G]Up, shepherd, [A7]and follow.
[D]Leave [G]your [D]ewes and [G]leave [Bm]your rams,
[D7]Rise [Em]Up, shepherd, [A7]and follow. [D]Follow, Follow,
[D]Rise [G]Up, shepherd, [D]and follow.
[D]Follow [C]the [G]star [A7]of Bethlehem,
[D]Rise [G]Up, shepherd, [D]and follow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]If you [G]take goo [A]heed tothe [D]angel's words,
[C]Rise [G]Up, shepherd, [A7]and follow.
[D]You'll [G]forget your [D]flocks, [G]you'll forget [Bm]your herds
[D7]Rise [Em]Up, [A7]shepherd, [D]and follow.
{end_of_verse}
